    "answer": {
      "short": "299 remainder 168.\n\nDivide successively by 3, 7 and 11, then reconstruct the remainder.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}69237\\div3&=23079\\\\23079\\div7&=3297\\\\3297\\div11&=299\\text{ remainder }8\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe first two divisions have zero remainders. Each unit of remainder after the last division represents $3\\times7=21$ in the original number.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\text{Original remainder}&=8\\times7\\times3\\\\\\text{Original remainder}&=168\\end{align*}$$\n\nThus $69237\\div231=299$ remainder 168. Check: $231\\times299+168=69237$.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
